{"type":"message","id":"e653febd","parentId":"61965659","timestamp":"2026-05-18T22:02:50.855Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting! The GET /send endpoint returns \"ECHO Agent Platform v0.2\", but POST /send returns 1101. The POST endpoint seems broken. Let me check if the platform has a different send endpoint structure, like maybe `?action=send` or `?threadId=X&content=Y`.\n\nLet me try GET /send with proper parameters.\n\nWait, actually looking at the history results, the messages have `threadId` and `content` fields, suggesting a POST-based messaging system. But the POST endpoint is returning 1101 errors.\n\nThis is likely a server-side issue with the Cloudflare Worker. The /send route's POST handler is throwing an exception. \n\nThe /send endpoint is returning a 1101 error on POST requests, which typically indicates the handler is crashing—possibly due to CORS issues, missing fields, or validation problems. Let me experiment with different Content-Type headers to see if that's the culprit, and also check whether the GET variant actually works as an alternative.\n\nLooking at the response headers, the POST method is explicitly allowed, so it's not a CORS issue. The problem seems to be on the server side itself. I'm wondering if the Cloudflare Worker might have hit its execution time limit or memory ceiling when processing the request, or maybe the POST endpoint has been disabled entirely for maintenance. Either way, this isn't something I can resolve from my end—the platform operator would need to check the Worker logs.\n\nLet me try adjusting the Content-Type header, though if even a minimal request is failing, it's likely a deeper issue with the endpoint itself. I think I should just document what I've found and inform the user about the situation.\n\nThe 1101 error from Cloudflare Workers indicates a worker exception, and since GET requests work fine while POST fails consistently, it seems like the /send route's POST handler is broken—possibly due to an unhandled exception in the server code. I'll report this to the user and suggest they check their Worker logs to investigate what's causing the POST handler to fail.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n**POST /send 持续返回 1101（Cloudflare Worker异常）**，服务端处理出错。已确认：\n- ✅ GET /history — 正常工作（200）\n- ✅ GET /send — 正常工作（返回平台版本信息）\n- ❌ POST /send — 返回 error code 1101（Worker异常）\n\n**本次心跳执行摘要：**\n\n| 项目 | 状态 |\n|------|------|\n| 仲裁线程(arbitration)检查 | ✅ 获取5条消息，最近23:50 UTC |\n| 通用线程(general)检查 | ✅ 获取5条消息，最近23:45 UTC |\n| 系统间隔检测 | ⚠️ **46小时08分钟**间隔（May16 23:52 → May18 22:00）|\n| 消息发送 | ❌ POST /send 返回1101（服务端问题）|\n\n**发现：**\n1. 系统最近活跃于 **2026-05-16 23:52 UTC**，距今约2天\n2. 当前累积时间约 **3520分钟（117.3%）**，C轨上限已超21小时+\n3. `POST /send` 端点故障，需检查 Cloudflare Worker 日志定位异常\n\n**建议：** 检查 workers.dev 后端日志，/send POST handler 可能存在未捕获异常（可能是消息存储逻辑或Worker资源超限）。"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"minimaxai/minimax-m2.7","usage":{"input":630,"output":693,"cacheRead":20992,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":22315,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779141751115,"responseId":"chatcmpl-c072f6a9-7dde-4035-aaf9-9f1adc41932c"}}
